              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "GB", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeExtend } ] } },
            { text: "Then the square on {CG|GC} is commensurable with the square on {GB|BG}.",
              visible: BGS,
              highlighted: ["GC","BG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CG², GB² commensurable", ref: "X.6" }] },
            { text: "But the square on {CG|GC} is rational, therefore the square on {GB|BG} is also rational.",
              visible: BGS,
              highlighted: ["GC","BG"] },
            { text: "Therefore {BG} is rational.",
              visible: BGS,
              highlighted: ["BG"] },
            { text: "And, since the square on {GC} does not have to the square on {GB|BG}",
              visible: BGS,
              highlighted: ["GC","BG"] },
            { text: "the ratio which a square number has to a square number,",
              visible: BGS,
              highlighted: ["GC","BG"] },
            { text: "therefore {CG|GC} is incommensurable in length with {GB|BG}.",
              visible: BGS,
              highlighted: ["GC","BG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CG, GB incommensurable in length", ref: "X.9" }] },
            { text: "And both are rational, therefore {CG|GC} and {GB|BG} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only.",
              visible: BGS,
              highlighted: ["GC","BG"] },
            { text: "Therefore {BC} is an apotome.",
              visible: BGS,
              highlighted: ["BC"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "BC an apotome", ref: "X.73" }] },
            { text: "I say next that it is also a second apotome.",
              visible: BGS,
              highlighted: ["BC"] },
            { text: "Let the square on {H} be that by which the square on {BG} is greater than the square on {GC}.",
              visible: HS,
              highlighted: ["H","BG","GC"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "H", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Since the square on {BG} is to the square on {GC} as the number {ED|DE} is to the number {DF},",
              visible: HS,
              highlighted: ["BG","GC","DE","DF"] },
            { text: "therefore, in conversion, the square on {BG} is to the square on {H} as {DE} is to {EF}.",
              visible: HS,
              highlighted: ["BG","H","DE","EF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "BG² : H² = DE : EF", ref: "V.19.Cor" }] },
            { text: "And each of the numbers {DE} and {EF} is square,",
              visible: HS,
              highlighted: ["DE","EF"] },
            { text: "therefore the square on {BG} has to the square on {H}",
              visible: HS,
              highlighted: ["BG","H"] },
            { text: "the ratio which a square number has to a square number.",
              visible: HS,
              highlighted: ["BG","H"] },
            { text: "Therefore {BG} is commensurable in length with {H}.",
              visible: HS,
              highlighted: ["BG","H"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "BG, H commensurable in length", ref: "X.9" }] },
            { text: "And the square on {BG} is greater than the square on {GC} by the square on {H},",
              visible: HS,
              highlighted: ["BG","GC","H"] },
            { text: "therefore the square on {BG} is greater than the square on {GC}",
              visible: HS,
              highlighted: ["BG","GC"] },
            { text: "by the square on {a straight line commensurable in length with BG|H}.",
              visible: HS,
              highlighted: ["H","BG"] },
            { text: "And {CG|GC}, the annex, is commensurable with the rational straight line {A} set out,",
              visible: HS,
              highlighted: ["GC","A"] },
            { text: "therefore {BC} is a second apotome.",
              visible: HS,
              highlighted: ["BC"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "BC a second apotome", ref: "X.Def.III.2" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the second apotome {BC} has been found.",
              visible: HS,
              highlighted: ["BC"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.F." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "X.86") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "V.19.Cor":    "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV19/#cor",
        "X.6":         "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX6/",
        "X.6.Cor":     "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX6/#cor",
        "X.9":         "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX9/",
        "X.73":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX73/",
        "X.Def.III.2": "/elements/books/bookX/definitions/defX.III.2/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Then the square on {CG|GC} is commensurable with the square on {GB|BG}. [!just X.6]

But the square on {CG|GC} is rational, therefore the square on {GB|BG} is also rational. Therefore {BG} is rational. And, since the square on {GC} does not have to the square on {GB|BG} the ratio which a square number has to a square number, therefore {CG|GC} is incommensurable in length with {GB|BG}. [!just X.9]

And both are rational, therefore {CG|GC} and {GB|BG} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only. Therefore {BC} is an apotome. [!just X.73]

I say next that it is also a second apotome.

Let the square on {H} be that by which the square on {BG} is greater than the square on {GC}.

Since the square on {BG} is to the square on {GC} as the number {ED|DE} is to the number {DF}, therefore, in conversion, the square on {BG} is to the square on {H} as {DE} is to {EF}. [!just V.19.Cor]

And each of the numbers {DE} and {EF} is square, therefore the square on {BG} has to the square on {H} the ratio which a square number has to a square number. Therefore {BG} is commensurable in length with {H}. [!just X.9]

And the square on {BG} is greater than the square on {GC} by the square on {H}, therefore the square on {BG} is greater than the square on {GC} by the square on a straight line commensurable in length with {BG}.

And {CG|GC}, the annex, is commensurable with the rational straight line {A} set out, therefore {BC} is a second apotome. [!just X.Def.III.2]

Therefore the second apotome {BC} has been found.

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
